Lumia 1520 (RM-940) -- WCD9320 codec core: both startup paths
Kernel 6.16.12, boot-1520-wcd9320-bringup2.img (r123), module bringup-rc2
2026-07-31

Precondition: /lib/modules purged before the boot, so nothing autoloaded and
the codec was neither powered nor enumerated. ADSP running, NGD registered,
DT-created device present with no driver bound.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
TEST 1 -- fresh bring-up (this driver owns power and reset)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  # modprobe wcd9320 handoff_on_remove=1

[110.669214] fresh bring-up: 7 supplies enabled, reset released
[110.669334] fresh bring-up: waiting for enumeration
[110.670425] device UP (#1), logical address 0xcb

  path=fresh online=1 adopted=0 power_owned=1
  reset_transitions=2 supply_enables=1 supply_disables=0
  identity_reads=1 identity_failures=0 stale_bus_state=0
  identity: major 0x0102 minor 0x0001 version 0x00 laddr 0xcb up 1 down 0

Two reset transitions (assert, release) and one supply enable: the driver
brought the part up itself, and the bus enumerated it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
STAGED HANDOFF -- unload leaving the hardware live
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

[120.759805] removing (fresh path, power_owned=1)
[120.760200] handoff: leaving the codec powered for the next driver

handoff_on_remove is research-only. It exists purely to construct the
condition late adoption is supposed to handle: a physically live codec plus
valid cached bus state. It must never become production behaviour.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
TEST 2 -- late adoption (codec genuinely live)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  # modprobe wcd9320          (handoff_on_remove=N)

[124.500324] bus reports enumerated (laddr 0xcb); verifying before adopting
[124.514279] late adoption: codec responded, no power or reset touched

  path=adopted online=1 adopted=1 power_owned=0
  reset_transitions=0 supply_enables=0 supply_disables=0
  identity_reads=1 identity_failures=0 stale_bus_state=0
  identity: major 0x0102 minor 0x0001 version 0x00 laddr 0xcb up 1 down 0

All three hardware counters are zero: the driver adopted a running codec
without touching power or reset. stale_bus_state=0 proves the verification
succeeded on the first path rather than the fallback rescuing it -- a stale
adoption could not have produced these numbers, because the fallback
increments that counter and drives reset.

