Unrelated pre-existing noise: qrtr / qcom_common / qmi_helpers "exports
duplicate symbol" from stale .ko files on the eMMC rootfs for subsystems this
build makes built-in. Cosmetic; clears when a matching rootfs is installed.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
What is NOT proven
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Codec-only hot removal remains unsupported. Unbinding a power-owning driver
powers the codec down while the SLIMbus core keeps reporting it UP, because
the remove path clears neither the cached status nor the logical address.
The driver now detects that on the next bind -- the identity read fails, the
stale state is counted, and it falls back to a controlled fresh bring-up --
but nothing client-side can make the remote ADSP manager forget its
assignment, so the fallback is allowed to fail honestly rather than loop.

Real re-enumeration belongs to controller-coordinated recovery: the NGD
driver marks its children absent during subsystem restart and re-queries them
after the master-capability exchange. Suspend/resume and an actual ADSP
restart are the right vehicles. Standalone codec power cycling is deferred.
